This extension adds Rocksmith 2014 Edition REMASTERED modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Includes functions to download all the tools you need. Works for LEARN AND PLAY edition.[/summary]

Includes functions to download all the tools you need.
[b][color=#b6d7a8][size=3]This also works for the LEARN &amp; PLAY version of the game.[/size][/color][/b]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Root Game Folder mods with a "base" folder or a "cache.psarc" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]CDLC mods with a ".psarc" file install to the "dlc" folder.[/*]
[*]Editor On Fire mods with an "eof.exe" file install to the "EditorOnFire" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[/list]

[b][size=3]Supported Tools:
[list]
[*]Essentials: [url=https://github.com/Lovrom8/RSMods]RSMods[/url]﻿, [url=https://ignition4.customsforge.com/tools/cdlcenabler]CDLC Enabler[/url]﻿﻿
[*]Optional: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/rocksmith2014editionremastered/mods/1]NoCableLauncher[/url]﻿, [url=https://github.com/mdias/rs_asio]RS_ASIO[/url], [url=https://asio4all.org/about/download-asio4all/]ASIO4ALL[/url]﻿, [url=https://ignition4.customsforge.com/tools/cfsm]CF Song Manager[/url]﻿
[*]Build Tools: [url=https://ignition4.customsforge.com/eof]Editor on Fire[/url]﻿, [url=https://github.com/iminashi/Rocksmith2014.NET]DLC Builder[/url]﻿[/size][/b]
[/list]
[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Rocksmith 2014 Edition REMASTERED mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods laid out the same way the files appear inside the game folder. Vortex copies the matched folder and everything under it straight into the game.

[code]
MyRootMod.zip
└── base\
    └── ... files in their real relative locations
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a folder named "base", "dlc", "guitarcade" or "venues" in the archive.
    - Recognised by a file named "cache.psarc", "audio.psarc", "crowd.psarc", "etudes.psarc", "gears.psarc", "guitars.psarc", "session.psarc", "songs.psarc", "static.psarc" or "video.psarc".

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders, instead of the game folders themselves, adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

CDLC Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".psarc" file.

  Installs to: "dlc"

========================================================================

Editor On Fire:

Recognised when the archive contains a "eof.exe" file.

  Installs to: "EditorOnFire"

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]
